+**Wrong-path fallback to origin-root `/metrics`.** The scraped URL is derived from your `--url`, so it can point at an API sub-path the normalizer cannot recognize — most often a complete inference URL passed as `--url` (e.g. `http://host:8000/v1/chat/completions`, which derives `.../v1/chat/completions/metrics`). OpenAI-compatible servers expose Prometheus at the origin root, so when the derived path answers non-200 during the reachability probe, AIPerf tries `http://host:8000/metrics` once and keeps scraping it if it responds:
